            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SunnyDaysNora"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These were delicious! I cooked for 35 minutes in oven, then cooked another 25 minutes, basting and turning wings every 5 minutes or so. If you don't like a super-saucy wing (like my husband) they're perfect just like that. If you love extra sauce, go crazy on top of that baked in flavor once they're done. Will definitely be making again. These aren't super-spicy as written, but like the directions say, it's easy to tweak the spiciness to your liking."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Chelsie Osenga"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a really good wing sauce recipe. I used Frank's buffalo sauce, instead of the Red Hot flavor because I didn't want it to be super spicy and it was perfect! The sauce takes a long time to cook, and I didn't notice that the first time I made this, but it's worth the wait! The addition of a fresh orange is key, don't leave it out!",
            "datePublished": "2017-04-29T17:43:08.533Z"
          },
